#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""vallum-desk — the self-service enrolment desk for a Vallum server.

One process on the server, next to the daemon. Anyone running a Vallum
server can point would-be users at it: a visitor signs up with an invite
code (closed alpha) or opens a paid plan later, receives an account number,
and enrols devices on demand — each device gets its own join ticket minted
by the daemon itself (ADR-0047: the account is not the device). The
operator never runs an SSH command per user.

    vallum-desk --config /etc/vallum/vallumrc.toml \
                --codes /etc/vallum/desk-codes.txt \
                --admin-token-file /etc/vallum/desk-admin-token \
                --bind 127.0.0.1 --port 8400

Binds loopback by default — put a TLS reverse proxy or an SSH tunnel in
front before exposing it. Runs as root because the daemon's control
socket is 0600 and peer operations are privileged; it speaks to the
daemon only through the `vallum` CLI, never by touching the config.

Plans (v1): trial with expiry and a byte cap, enforced by a sweep thread
that reads the daemon's per-peer counters. Payment integration attaches
at the plan boundary — the schema keeps a `paid_until` and `plan` field
so a billing webhook only ever updates a row.

Structure: `Desk` holds the account lifecycle and depends on a `Daemon`
port, so the daemon can be faked in tests; `DaemonCli` is the one
implementation that talks to the CLI.

SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
"""

import argparse
